        "id": "300",
        "title": "COMPUTER NETWORK TECHNOLOGY",
        "description": "Contestants will demonstrate foundational and advanced knowledge of modern computer networking, including architectures, protocols, hardware, connectivity, and security. Core competencies assessed include, but are not limited to, Design, configure, and troubleshoot computer networks using OSI/TCP-IP models, subnetting, and IPv4/IPv6 addressing to ensure scalable and secure connectivity; Install, configure, and troubleshoot computer hardware components to ensure reliable performance and minimize downtime in networked environments.",
