        "description": "Contestants will demonstrate knowledge of fundamental web design coding and syntax to include CSS3 and HTML5 standards. Core competencies assessed include, but are not limited to, Develop and maintain web pages using semantic HTML5 and CSS3 standards, applying responsive typography, layout, and formatting techniques to ensure accessibility, SEO, and consistent branding across devices; Implement Web Content Accessibility Guidelines and ensure cross-browser compatibility using progressive enhancement and testing tools to deliver inclusive and consistent user experiences.",
        "wsapLink": "#",
        "practiceTests": [],
        "generatorLink": "#"
    },
    "365": {
        "id": "365",
        "title": "WEBSITE DESIGN AND DEVELOPMENT TEAM",
        "description": "Contestants will create a website based on the topic provided. Core competencies assessed include, but are not limited to, Apply audience analysis and design principles and elements to create intuitive navigation, engaging content, and effective page layouts using UX/UI best practices, ensuring accessibility and visual appeal across devices and platforms; Assess project requirements and delegate tasks effectively within multidisciplinary teams, utilizing project management tools, agile methodologies, and collaborative workflows to create and maintain high-quality, SEO-optimized site content.",
        "wsapLink": "#",
        "practiceTests": [],
        "generatorLink": "#"
    },
    "390": {
        "id": "390",
        "title": "DIGITAL TECHNOLOGY CONCEPTS (OPEN)",
        "description": "Contestants will demonstrate foundational knowledge of the information technology field, including core concepts across hardware, software, operating systems, networking, security, and technology applications. Core competencies assessed include, but are not limited to, Demonstrate foundational understanding of core IT concepts, including hardware, software, operating systems, and networking, and apply practical skills to configure, manage, and troubleshoot these components for secure and efficient operations; Explain the evolution of programming languages and apply this knowledge to evaluate language paradigms, features, and appropriate use cases when selecting technologies for various projects.",
        "wsapLink": "#",
